# EduRepo – Cline Project Rules

These rules exist to prevent recurring issues from past sessions. Read them fully
before making changes, and re-check the "Known Pitfalls" section before touching
Docker, Prisma, or environment configuration.

## Project Overview

- **Purpose**: Educational material repository/sharing platform for Swiss teachers (Lehrplan 21).
- **Stack**: Next.js 14 (App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, `next-intl`, `next-themes`) frontend ·
  NestJS 10 + Prisma backend · PostgreSQL 16 · Redis 7 · MinIO (S3) · Docker Compose.
- **Docs & comments are written in German** (README, docs/, inline comments).
  Keep new comments/docs consistent with the surrounding language.
- Relevant docs: `README.md`, `docs/RUNNING.md` (operations + troubleshooting),
  `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md`, `docs/METADATA.md`.

## Repository Layout

```
backend/          NestJS API (src/), Prisma schema + seed (prisma/), Dockerfile, docker-entrypoint.sh
frontend/         Next.js app (src/app/[locale]/...), messages (src/messages/{de,en,fr,it}.json)
docker-compose.yml        PRODUCTION compose (default) – self-contained images, NO source mounts
docker-compose.dev.yml    DEV overlay (hot-reload) – only used together with docker-compose.yml
.env.example      Template – MUST stay in sync with docker-compose.yml variables
.env              Local secrets – gitignored, NEVER commit
```

## Commands (always run from repo root `/opt/src/EduRepo`)

```bash
# Production build & start (default):
docker compose up -d --build

# Development (hot-reload) – overlay is MANDATORY for dev:
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d --build

# Logs / status:
docker compose ps
docker compose logs -f backend

# Validate all buildable images (backend + frontend, prod stage):
docker compose build

# Validate dev stages as well:
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.dev.yml build
```

- **No lock files are committed** (`npm install`, no `package-lock.json`). Keep it that way;
  do not run `npm ci`.
- Node images are `node:20-bookworm-slim`; backend needs `openssl`, `python3`, `make`, `g++`
  (argon2/Prisma engines) in build stages only.
- Frontend prod build expects `output: 'standalone'` (`next.config.mjs`) and starts `node server.js`.

## Verification Workflow (MANDATORY)

1. After changing **Dockerfiles, package.json, compose files, or anything affecting the build**:
   run `docker compose build` and confirm it succeeds. If dev-relevant, also build dev stages.
2. After changing **backend/frontend source**: rebuild and start the stack, then check
   `docker compose ps` (all services Up/healthy) and scan `docker compose logs backend frontend`
   for errors before declaring success.
3. After changing **Prisma schema** (`backend/prisma/schema.prisma`): the entrypoint applies it
   via `prisma migrate deploy` (if `prisma/migrations/` exists) else `prisma db push`, then runs
   the idempotent seed (`node dist/prisma/seed.js`). Restart backend to re-apply.
4. Never claim "done" while a container is crash-looping. Check logs and fix the root cause.

## Known Pitfalls – DO NOT reintroduce these

### Docker / Deployment
- **NEVER bind-mount source code in the production compose** (`docker-compose.yml`).
  Mounting `./backend:/app` or `./frontend:/app` on servers without a checkout caused
  `ENOENT: /app/package.json` and `Could not find Prisma Schema`. Source mounts live
  ONLY in `docker-compose.dev.yml`.
- **MinIO/mc image versions are deliberately pinned** (`minio/minio:RELEASE.2022-10-24T18-35-07Z`,
  `minio/mc:RELEASE.2023-01-11T03-14-16Z`) because the target host CPU lacks x86-64-v2 support;
  newer releases crash with `Fatal glibc error`. Do NOT "update" them unless the host changes.
  Overridable via `MINIO_IMAGE` / `MC_IMAGE`.
- **`minio-init` is a long-running health-guard, NOT a one-shot job.** It creates the bucket
  (idempotent), touches `/tmp/bucket-init.ok`, then stays alive via `exec tail -f /dev/null`;
  its healthcheck (`test -f /tmp/bucket-init.ok`) gates the backend (`depends_on:
  condition: service_healthy`). This keeps the whole stack "Up (healthy)" in `docker compose ps`.
  Do NOT convert it back to a one-shot (`restart: "no"` + exit) service and do NOT remove its
  healthcheck – an exited init container made the stack report unhealthy/exited.
- **`NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables are baked into the frontend image at build time.**
  Changing them requires `docker compose up -d --build frontend`.
- **Browser talks same-origin only**: Next.js rewrites `/api/*` → `API_INTERNAL_URL`
  (default `http://backend:4000`). Keep `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` empty by default. Setting it to
  an unreachable host causes "Failed to fetch" / CORS / mixed-content errors.
- **S3 credentials**: In `docker-compose.yml`, `S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`/`S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` default
  to `MINIO_ROOT_USER`/`MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD`. Leave `S3_*` unset in `.env` unless a dedicated
  service account exists – mismatches caused `SignatureDoesNotMatch`/`InvalidAccessKeyId`.
- **Do not swallow errors** (e.g. `.catch(() => false)`) in initialization paths (storage,
  minio-init, migrations) – this produced cryptic cascading failures. Fail fast with a clear,
  actionable diagnostic message instead.
- Data persistence: volumes live under `${EDUREPO_DATA_DIR:-./docker-data}` (Coder workspace:
  `/opt/coder/EduRepo/docker-data`). After a workspace update the IP may change – then update
  `PUBLIC_BASE_URL`, `API_BASE_URL`, `CORS_ORIGINS`, `S3_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT` in `.env`.

### Backend (NestJS + Prisma)
- Seed must stay **idempotent** (upsert catalogs; create admin only if missing; random admin
  password is printed to logs once).
- `prisma/seed.ts` is compiled to `dist/prisma/seed.js` (tsconfig includes `prisma/**/*.ts`;
  `rootDir: "."` → `dist/src/main.js`). If build output paths change, update
  `backend/docker-entrypoint.sh` and `package.json` scripts together.
- `npm prune --omit=dev` can delete the generated Prisma client – the prod Dockerfile
  re-runs `npx prisma generate` after pruning. Preserve this.
- Env vars consumed by the backend are declared in `docker-compose.yml` – when adding one,
  also add it to `.env.example` (with a safe default or comment) and keep
  compose defaults in sync.

### Frontend (Next.js)
- **i18n: all four locales** (`de`, `en`, `fr`, `it`) in `frontend/src/messages/*.json` must
  receive every new translation key. Never update only one locale file.
- Routes live under `src/app/[locale]/`; use helpers from `src/i18n/` for links/redirects.
- Auth uses an httpOnly cookie (`access_token`) set by the backend – API calls from the browser
  must go through the same-origin `/api` proxy, not direct backend URLs.

### Git / Terminal
- **Avoid interactive pagers**: use `git --no-pager <cmd>` or append `| cat` (a hung pager
  blocked previous sessions). Prefer non-interactive commands (`-y`, `--no-pager`, etc.).
- Never commit `.env`, `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `.next/`, or `docker-data/`.
  Check `git status` before committing.
- Commit message style: Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`, …), English,
  with a body explaining the "why" for non-trivial changes (see `git log` for examples).

## Task Etiquette

- Start every task by exploring the codebase; don't assume structure.
- Keep changes minimal and consistent with existing style (German comments, file naming,
  module layout under `backend/src/<feature>/`, feature pages under `frontend/src/app/[locale]/`).
- After finishing, verify with the workflow under "Verification Workflow" and summarize
  what was changed, built, and how it was validated.